UNIT annotations_text
KIND FUNCTIONAL
FIDELITY package
ANCHOR rederive@9e2245be5f42 cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs annotations — the GitHub workflow-command lines for the review findings; reproduce the code exactly, accidents included
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG annotations_text(findings: list[json]) -> text
ENVELOPE findings is a list; each element is normally a map holding level, path, line, title and message, but any json
  element is in scope (R1: an element that is not a map is skipped). Field values are any json. Text is well-formed
  Unicode (no lone surrogate). Values outside the abstract types (a findings value that is not a list, a host value with
  no json meaning) belong to the js file's envelope widening. Throws are IN scope as observations: R6 says where; the
  message is not graded.
DEPENDS-ON none
DESCRIPTION Render the review's findings as GitHub Actions workflow commands, one line per finding, so the runner shows
  each as a check annotation. A finding { level, path, line, title, message } becomes
  "::" LEVEL " file=" PROP(path) [",line=" LINE] ",title=" PROP(title) "::" DATA(message). This is the injection
  boundary: text from a contract reaches stdout here and the runner executes any line that starts with "::", so every
  value a contract controls is escaped (path and title as properties, message as data) and the two values that are not
  escaped (level and line) are held to a fixed domain. The two escapes are restated here (DEPENDS-ON none). The contract
  assumes, and does not check, that the runner splits its output into lines on CR and LF only (PINNED LINE-BREAKS-ESCAPED).
BEHAVIOR
R1 KEPT = the elements of findings that are maps, in list order; every other element (none, text, number, bool, list) is
  skipped and leaves no line and no separator. The result is the rendered line of each element of KEPT, in order, joined
  by a single LF (U+000A); no LF before the first line or after the last. An empty KEPT (the empty list, or a list of
  skipped elements only) yields the empty text; one kept element yields its line with no LF at all. CITED FIDELITY package — the fix of 9e2245be5f42: one bad element never aborts the output
R2 FIELD(e, k) for a kept element e is the value e holds under key k, or ABSENT when e has no key k. ABSENT and none read
  alike everywhere below.
R3 Each line is, in exactly this order with no other separator or whitespace: "::", LEVEL, " file=", PROP(TEXT-OF(path)),
  then LINE-PART, then ",title=", PROP(TEXT-OF(title)), "::", DATA(TEXT-OF(message)). path, title and message are
  FIELD(e, "path"), FIELD(e, "title"), FIELD(e, "message"). The file property and the title property are always written,
  with an empty value when their field is ABSENT or none.
R4 LEVEL is FIELD(e, "level") when that is exactly the text error, warning or notice (case-sensitive, no trimming);
  anything else (another text, a non-text value, ABSENT) gives the text "error", so an unknown level fails toward the
  most visible annotation. LEVEL is never escaped. CITED FIDELITY package — kept by ruling (F8)
R5 LINE-PART: let L = FIELD(e, "line"). When L is a number with no fractional part and 1 <= L <= 9007199254740991
  (2^53 - 1, the largest SAFE integer), LINE-PART is ",line=" followed by L as plain decimal digits (no sign, no point, no
  exponent). Otherwise LINE-PART is empty: ABSENT, none, text (also "3"), bool, list, map, NaN, an infinity, zero,
  negative zero, a negative number, a fraction, and every number from 2^53 up (9007199254740992, 1e21) all omit it.
  CITED FIDELITY package — the fix of 9e2245be5f42 (F2): only a safe positive integer is written
R6 TEXT-OF(v), the text a field value renders as, by TABLE TEXT-OF. Coercion applies before escaping.
TABLE TEXT-OF — v is a field value (or ABSENT)
  ABSENT or none                        | the empty text (never "undefined" or "null")
  bool                                  | "true" or "false"
  text                                  | itself, unchanged
  number                                | NUM-TEXT(v) (R7)
  list                                  | the TEXT-OF of each element joined by "," with no spaces; an element that is none renders as the empty text; a nested list renders by the same rule (so [[1,[2]],3] gives 1,2,3); the empty list gives the empty text
  map without an own key toString       | the text "[object Object]" (its entries never matter; a key valueOf alone does not change this)
  map with an own key toString          | throws, for the whole call (whatever that key holds, none included), whether at the top or nested inside a list at any depth CITED FIDELITY package — kept by ruling (F4): the host's text conversion finds a toString member that is not callable, and the map's other members yield no primitive; only text reaches this code from the review
R7 NUM-TEXT(x) is the shortest round-trip decimal text of the double x in the ECMAScript Number-to-String form: NaN gives
  "NaN"; the infinities give "Infinity" and "-Infinity"; both zeros give "0" (no sign); otherwise a leading - for a negative,
  then, with k significant digits s and decimal exponent n (value = s * 10^(n-k), s the shortest digit string that reads
  back as x): plain digits with no point when k <= n <= 21 (trailing zeros padded: 1e20 gives 100000000000000000000);
  a point after the first n digits when 0 < n < k; "0." then -n zeros then the digits when -6 < n <= 0 (0.000001); otherwise
  exponent form: the first digit, then "." and the rest when k > 1, then "e", then "+" or "-", then the decimal |n-1|
  (1e+21, 1e-7, 1.7976931348623157e+308). There is never a trailing ".0" and never a leading "+" on the mantissa.
R8 PROP(t), the property escape for path and title, replaces in t, character by character, using TABLE ESCAPES column
  PROP; DATA(t), the data escape for message, uses column DATA. Every other character, including U+2028, U+2029, U+0085,
  TAB, VT, FF, "=", "::"-forming colons in DATA and every non-ASCII character, passes unchanged. The replacement is one
  pass over the original characters: an inserted "%" is never escaped again, so "%0A" in the input becomes "%250A" and a
  real LF becomes "%0A". CITED FIDELITY package — the code runs the replacements in sequence with "%" first, which is equivalent
TABLE ESCAPES — character | PROP | DATA
  % (U+0025)  | %25 | %25
  CR (U+000D) | %0D | %0D
  LF (U+000A) | %0A | %0A
  : (U+003A)  | %3A | unchanged
  , (U+002C)  | %2C | unchanged
PINNED charset LINE-BREAKS-ESCAPED = { U+000A, U+000D } CITED R8 — the only line-break characters either escape removes; ASSUMED (kept by ruling, F5): the runner splits its output on exactly these
INVARIANT no rendered line contains CR or LF, so the result holds exactly one line per kept element (an LF only between lines).
INVARIANT each line starts with "::" then error, warning or notice, then " file="; the text between " file=" and the
  second "::" of the line contains no colon and holds only the properties the code writes (file, an optional line,
  title), because PROP removes every colon and comma from path and title.
INVARIANT the hex digits of every escape are uppercase.
ORACLE value -> oracles/annotations_text.json  CANONICAL-SHA256 246a4ea6961a89cbd37b26e7f2372036ce7db4f8d8df914ee59d1306a4de7193
SCOPE IN: R1–R8 over any list of json elements, including the throw of R6. OUT: printing the result (the caller
  writes it to stdout), the review that produces the findings, and what the GitHub runner does with each line.
NOTE rust omitted. Cause: domain — the review system ships as JavaScript (rdv review and the rederive/sir-review GitHub Action); there is no Rust consumer.
PROVENANCE rederive@9e2245be5f42 (MIT) cli/lsp/pr-review.mjs: annotations, val, escapeProperty, escapeData, LEVELS. Cut
  2026-11-02 in the v0.5 contract register for the review system's self-treatment, phase 2; revised the same day on the
  architect's rulings (F1 F2 F3 fixed in the code; F4 F5 F6 F7 F8 F9 kept).
